{"name":"Rowntree","hex":"#8e8e6e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rowntree","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rowntree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rowntree's","blocks":[{"text":"Nestlé UK Ltd., trading as Rowntree's, is a British confectionery brand and a former business based in York, England. Rowntree developed Fruit Pastilles, Kit Kat, Aero, Smarties, After Eight thin mint chocolates, and acquired the Rolo and Quality Street brands when it merged with Mackintosh's in 1969 to form Rowntree Mackintosh Confectionery. The Yorkie and Lion bars were introduced in 1976. Rowntree's also pioneered festive selection boxes which in the UK have been a staple gift at Christmas for over a century."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a8/Rowntree%27s_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rowntree's","wikidata":"Q695070"},{"title":"Rowntree trusts","blocks":[{"text":"The four Rowntree Trusts are funded from the legacies of the Quaker chocolate entrepreneurs and social reformers Joseph Rowntree and\nBenjamin Seebohm Rowntree. The trusts are based in the Rowntrees' home city of\nYork, England. The trusts are:"},{"items":["the Joseph Rowntree Charitable Trust, a Quaker philanthropic trust;","the Joseph Rowntree Foundation, which funds social policy research and development;","the Joseph Rowntree Housing Trust, which owns and manages the model village of New Earswick, and a number of other housing schemes in the York area;","the Joseph Rowntree Reform Trust, which is a political body and promotes democratic reform and social justice within the UK. Unlike the other three, it is not a charity, though it endowed the JRSST Charitable Trust."]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rowntree_trusts","wikidata":"Q7372268"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Joseph_rowntree_old.jpg/250px-Joseph_rowntree_old.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fb/Joseph_rowntree_old.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Joseph_rowntree_old.jpg/250px-Joseph_rowntree_old.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Joseph Rowntree became owner of the company when his brother and founder, Henry, died in 1883.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoseph_rowntree_old.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Rowntree%27s_Cocoa_-_TWCMS-G11480_%2816692709351%29.jpg/500px-Rowntree%27s_Cocoa_-_TWCMS-G11480_%2816692709351%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Rowntree%27s_Cocoa_-_TWCMS-G11480_%2816692709351%29.jpg/500px-Rowntree%27s_Cocoa_-_TWCMS-G11480_%2816692709351%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rowntree's Cocoa tin manufactured between 1936 and 1941","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARowntree's_Cocoa_-_TWCMS-G11480_(16692709351).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/HK_Shau_Kei_Wan_%E9%A6%99%E6%B8%AF%E6%B5%B7%E9%98%B2%E5%8D%9A%E7%89%A9%E9%A4%A8_Museum_of_Coastal_Defence_HKMCD_British_foods_1940s_Rowntree%27s_Kit_Kat_Chocolate.JPG/500px-HK_Shau_Kei_Wan_%E9%A6%99%E6%B8%AF%E6%B5%B7%E9%98%B2%E5%8D%9A%E7%89%A9%E9%A4%A8_Museum_of_Coastal_Defence_HKMCD_British_foods_1940s_Rowntree%27s_Kit_Kat_Chocolate.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/HK_Shau_Kei_Wan_%E9%A6%99%E6%B8%AF%E6%B5%B7%E9%98%B2%E5%8D%9A%E7%89%A9%E9%A4%A8_Museum_of_Coastal_Defence_HKMCD_British_f